From 7deab5e44f2fbb24e5fa77e7741afac68efd11cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:10:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CI: gradlew Permission denied (exit 126) on the AAB build

The release-bundle step started failing with "./gradlew: Permission
denied" - the file is committed with the executable bit set (100755),
but that bit doesn't reliably survive a Windows git client, a patch
applied with git apply instead of git am, or a manual re-save, and it
had been silently flipped back to non-executable by the time this ran
in CI. Added an unconditional `chmod +x gradlew` step right before the
build runs, so this doesn't depend on whatever mode happens to be
tracked by the time a commit is pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0117Yza2cLL621d3pHBjry2q
---
 .github/workflows/build-apk.yml | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build-apk.yml b/.github/workflows/build-apk.yml
index 657651f..3599d0d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build-apk.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build-apk.yml
@@ -39,6 +39,18 @@ jobs:
         # gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties), so ./gradlew drives the
         # version; this action is kept for its build-cache/daemon setup.
 
+      - name: Make gradlew executable
+        # gradlew is committed with the executable bit set (100755), but
+        # that bit doesn't survive every path a commit can take before it
+        # reaches this checkout - a Windows git client, a patch applied
+        # with `git apply` instead of `git am`, or a manual re-save can all
+        # silently flip it back to 100644, which fails here with "Permission
+        # denied" (exit 126) rather than anywhere closer to the cause. Doing
+        # this unconditionally means the build never depends on whatever the
+        # tracked mode happens to be by the time it's pushed.
+        working-directory: EduQuinn-Android-Build-Ready/EduQuinn-Android
+        run: chmod +x gradlew
+
       - name: Decode signing keystore
         working-directory: EduQuinn-Android-Build-Ready/EduQuinn-Android
         run: echo "${{ secrets.KEYSTORE_BASE64 }}" | base64 -d > app/release.jks
